      "message": "Typically you would just query the version and then from there you know what features are available, you\u0027re also versioning the ioctls ie. ZRAM_ANDROID_IOC_PROCESS_WRITEBACK_V0.\n\nUserfaultfd(2) does something similar:\n\nhttps://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man2/userfaultfd.2.html\n\n```\n              Programs that *do* should call UFFDIO_API twice: once with\n              `features \u003d 0` to detect features supported by this kernel, and\n              again with the subset of features the program actually wants to\n              enable.  */\n           uffdio_api.api \u003d UFFD_API;\n           uffdio_api.features \u003d 0;\n           if (ioctl(uffd, UFFDIO_API, \u0026uffdio_api) \u003d\u003d -1)\n               err(EXIT_FAILURE, \"ioctl-UFFDIO_API\");\n```\n\nIn our case we would just query for a version or \"features\" and from there know what userspace is able to do.",
